# Native per-expert kernels for Flash-Next's formats, IQ3_XXS gate/up and
# IQ4_NL down (IQ4_XS down shares the layout and the path): a lane decodes a whole 32-value block per step (the shape of
# llama.cpp's vec_dot_iq3_xxs_q8_1), eight values at a time into f32 weights
# that every token of a tile takes, against f16 activations with f32 sums (no
# activation quantisation). The IQ3_XXS grid is an f32 table in constant
# memory and its signs come from the 7-bit index and its parity; IQ4_NL
# values are picked by two selects over the table held in registers. A
# block's sum is one fma chain over its 32 values, its scale factored out
# (acc = fma(scale, block sum, acc)). The summation order changes against
# 0061's per-element decoders, so the bytes differ from theirs, inside the
# CPU-oracle band; a token's bytes stay the same across the per-pair, batched
# and grouped kinds. Gate/up runs 2 rows per subgroup (MOE_NATIVE_GU_ROWS=
# 1|2|4); the down gives each row a group of 4 lanes. MOE_NATIVE_LEGACY_DECODE
# =1 keeps 0061's decoders in the same build; the weight-rounding arm always
# does. IQ2_S, IQ2_S-packed, IQ4_NL gate/up, Q8_0 and the IQ3_XXS down are
# untouched. A770, one block at hidden 2560 / inter 640, 16 experts, top-10,
# weights in device memory: T=1 gate/up 280.9 -> 79.0 us, down 74.3 -> 34.3
# us per call; T=128 (grouped) gate/up 11655 -> 3797 us, down 2222 -> 1406 us.
#
