+// arcint (patch 0069): whole-block decoders for the IQ3_XXS gate/up and the
+// IQ4_NL down (the Flash-Next formats). The per-element decoders above give
+// each lane two values of a 32-block, each with its own byte load, table load
+// and activation load. Here a lane decodes a whole 32-value block from one
+// 8-byte grid-index load (IQ3_XXS) or one 16-byte code load (IQ4_NL), as
+// llama.cpp's vec_dot_iq3_xxs_q8_1 does, but the activations stay f16 -> f32
+// and the sums f32: no activation quantisation. A block is decoded eight
+// values at a time into f32 weights (the IQ3_XXS grid is held as f32, so a
+// lookup is one vector load and no byte unpacking), and every token of a tile
+// takes the same decoded weights. A block's sum is ONE fma chain over its 32
+// values in order (s = fma(x_k, w_k, s) from s = 0), and the block's scale is
+// factored out of it (acc = fma(scale, s, acc)), so the summation order
+// differs from the per-element decoders' (x * scale * magnitude * sign per
+// element, lane-strided): the bytes differ from theirs, inside the CPU-oracle
+// band. Every sum is written with explicit fma, so -cl-mad-enable has no
+// contraction left to choose per kernel variant; that a token's bytes do not
+// depend on the variant is measured by the cells of
+// tests/python/test_native_lowering_gpu.py (batched and grouped == per pair; a
+// token's bytes do not depend on its call). These helpers read no JIT
+// constant: they are compiled once per program whatever formats its sources
+// carry.
